κατ-αρτίζω 
 [in LXX chiefly in Ps (Psa.8:2 al.; כּוּן, etc.) and Ezra (כְּלַל) ;] 
to render ἄρτιος, i.e. fit, complete; 
 __(a) to mend, repair: Mat.4:21, Mrk.1:19; 
 __(b) to furnish completely, complete, equip, prepare: pass., Luk.6:40, Rom.9:22, Heb.11:3; mid., Mat.21:16 (LXX), Heb.10:5 (LXX); 
 __(with) in ethical sense, to prepare, complete, perfect: Gal.6:1 (EV, restore), 1Pe.5:10; pass., 1Co.1:10 (Field, Notes, 167), 2Co.13:11, Heb.13:21 (cf. προ-καταρτίζω).†
 (AS)

A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.13; 
 son of: Othniel (H6274) whose wife was Achsah (H5915); 
 brother of: Meonothai (H4587)(?) 
 § Hathath = "fearful"
 son of Othniel and grandson of Kenaz, the brother of Caleb

A man of the tribe of Asher living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.34; 
 son of: Shomer (H7763H); 
 brother of: Ahi (H0277H), Jehubbah (H3160) and Aram (H0758J) 
 § Rohgah = "clamour"
 an Asherite of the sons of Shamer

A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Rut.4.20; 
 son of: Nahshon (H5177); 
 husband of: Rahab (H7343); 
 father of: Boaz (H1162); also called Sala at Luk.3.32; 
Another spelling of sal.ma (שַׂלְמָא "Salmon" H8007) 
 § Salmon = "garment"
1) father of Boaz, father-in-law of Ruth, and grandfather of David
1a) also 'Salmah', 'Salma'
